<title>POLAND: Poles with bank accounts rises to 31 pct - poll.</title>
<headline>Poles with bank accounts rises to 31 pct - poll.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The percentage of persons holding a bank account in Poland rose last year by nearly one half to 31 percent, a report released on Friday by the private Pentor polling institute showed.</p>
<p>In February last year 20 percent of Poles had accounts.</p>
<p>The report also said 55 percent of Poles at the start of this year deemed the zloty a solid currency worthy of trust.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
